# Comment-layer config, loaded in EVERY mode — `npm run dev` and the Vercel
# production build read this same file, so both talk to the same BB PM
# backend (`pm.burningbros.kr`). There is no separate dev instance of BB PM,
# which is deliberate: the passcode flow, the OAuth flow and the comment data
# behave locally exactly as they do deployed.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, READ THIS ONCE
#
# A comment you post while developing is a REAL comment in the SRM project.
# Everyone with the link sees it, and if you were signed in with BB PM it is
# an internal thread carrying your name. Delete your test threads when you're
# done — the rail's trash icon is enough.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS COMMITTED, AND WHY THAT'S SAFE
#
# Vite inlines `VITE_*` at build time, and the Vercel project hosting this
# site belongs to another account — contributors here have repo write but no
# dashboard access, so committing the values is the only route that doesn't
# depend on someone else.
#
# None of them is a secret. The share token is half a credential and ships in
# the client bundle regardless: anyone can read it out of the deployed JS. The
# *passcode* is the actual gate, and it is never in this file, in the bundle,
# or in the repo. The OAuth client id belongs to a **public** client — no
# secret exists for it, and PKCE is what proves a code exchange belongs to the
# browser that started the flow.
#
# That split holds only while the passcode is strong. If it leaks, rotate it:
# BB PM → project → Share links → Manage → key icon → Generate → Save.
# Rotating does NOT change the token, so nothing here needs editing.
#
# NEVER put a `bbpm_...` API key in here. That one is a full-account
# credential and would be readable by anyone who opens the page.

# ─── Where the comments live ────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_BBPM_API_BASE=https://pm.burningbros.kr/api

# Token of the COMMENT-scoped share link on the SRM project. Blank it and the
# whole comment layer compiles out — the site behaves exactly as it did before
# comments existed (see `commentsConfigured` in `src/comments/client.ts`).
VITE_BBPM_SHARE_TOKEN=16574965e46951bb100306f6cc73fd52

# ─── Team sign-in ("Continue with BB PM") ───────────────────────────────────
#
# Registered for exactly two redirect URIs, and the authorization server
# refuses every other one:
#
#   https://saramin-eta.vercel.app/oauth/callback   production
#   http://localhost:5173/oauth/callback            npm run dev
#
# So sign-in works locally against production BB PM with no extra setup —
# `localhost` is a secure context (PKCE needs one) and the API allows any
# localhost origin through CORS without being told to.
#
# Two things this does NOT cover:
#   · A Vercel *preview* deployment gets a one-off origin, so previews fall
#     back to the passcode. Same for a dev server on any port but 5173 —
#     hence `--strictPort` in the dev script, so it fails loudly instead of
#     drifting to 5174 and breaking sign-in in a way that looks like a bug.
#   · A new domain needs its own registration: see README → Comments.
#
# Blank this and the dialog quietly offers the passcode alone.
VITE_BBPM_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=bbpm_client_c6bed652395b0b7fe35a97023e0c097a
